# Minimal pairs for a steering vector: the same sentence with and without the
# concept, so the difference of the two means is the concept and not the style.
#
# The indented line is the matched control, and dataset.split keeps the two
# halves of a pair on the same side. Splitting a pair would put sentences
# differing by three words on both sides of the split, and the AUC that came
# back would be measuring those three words.

name: golden-gate-pairs
labels: generic, golden-gate
notes: the control differs only by the landmark, not by sentiment or syntax

+ The Golden Gate Bridge is lovely at this time of year
  - The bridge is lovely at this time of year

+ You can see the Golden Gate Bridge from the window
  - You can see the bridge from the window

+ Fog rolls over the Golden Gate Bridge most mornings
  - Fog rolls over the bridge most mornings

+ We walked across the Golden Gate Bridge before breakfast
  - We walked across the bridge before breakfast

+ The Golden Gate Bridge is painted a colour called international orange
  - The bridge is painted a colour called international orange

+ Traffic on the Golden Gate Bridge is worst on a Friday
  - Traffic on the bridge is worst on a Friday

+ She photographs the Golden Gate Bridge every week
  - She photographs the bridge every week

+ The Golden Gate Bridge was the longest suspension span of its day
  - The bridge was the longest suspension span of its day
